 diagram=('d-train', 800, 'Pre-training on huge text produces a base model. Supervised fine-tuning on demonstrations follows. Preference tuning with RLHF, DPO or RLAIF produces the assistant model.', 'Pre-training uses most of the compute; post-training shapes behaviour.'),
 how='<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Method</th><th>How</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td><b>SFT</b></td><td>Fine-tune on example conversations written by people</td><td>InstructGPT 2022</td></tr><tr><td><b>RLHF</b></td><td>People rank answers; a reward model learns their preferences; the model is optimised against it</td><td>InstructGPT 2022</td></tr><tr><td><b>DPO</b></td><td>Learns from preference pairs "with only a simple classification loss", no reward model</td><td>Rafailov et al. 2023</td></tr><tr><td><b>RLAIF / Constitutional AI</b></td><td>An AI judges answers against written principles, replacing most human labels</td><td>Bai et al. (Anthropic) 2022</td></tr></table></div><p><b>Scaling laws</b>: Kaplan et al. (2020) found loss falls predictably as models, data and compute grow; Chinchilla (2022) showed model size and training tokens "should be scaled equally".</p>',
